---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';

const PAGE_TITLE = 'HardWhere | Steven Brennan';
const PAGE_DESCRIPTION = 'HardWhere project page showcasing gameplay programming work, technical highlights, and development experience.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={PAGE_TITLE} description={PAGE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />

		<main id="main">
			<section class="project-hero" aria-labelledby="project-title">
				<video
					class="project-hero-video"
					poster="/HardWhere_Poster.png"
					autoplay
					muted
					loop
					playsinline
					preload="none"
					aria-hidden="true"
				>
					<source src="/HardGameplayLoop.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
				</video>

				<div class="project-hero-overlay" aria-hidden="true"></div>

				<div class="project-hero-content">
					<img
						class="project-title-image"
						src="/HardWhereTitleCard.png"
						alt="HardWhere title card"
					/>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="project-section">
				<h2 class="sr-only" id="project-title">HardWhere</h2>
				<p class="project-summary">
					Navigate rooms and solve the puzzles within by controlling a Robot who must make use of his own detached head! Just don't stray too far, or you may lose signal.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="project-section" aria-labelledby="video-title">
				<div class="project-video-wrap">
					<iframe
						class="project-video"
						src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/_QQU2f2vGpE?autoplay=1&mute=1&rel=0&playsinline=1"
						title="HardWhere gameplay video"
						allow="autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture"
						allowfullscreen
					></iframe>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="project-section" aria-labelledby="skills-title">
				<h2 id="skills-title">Skills Used:</h2>
				<div class="project-tags">
					<span class="project-tag">Unity</span>
					<span class="project-tag">C#</span>
					<span class="project-tag">Gameplay Programming</span>
					<span class="project-tag">Systems Design</span>
					<span class="project-tag">Level Design</span>
					<span class="project-tag">UI</span>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="project-section" aria-labelledby="overview-title">
				<h2 id="overview-title">Overview:</h2>
				<p>
					HardWhere? Was my Final Year Project artefact, utilising a Second-Person perspective to solve and escape puzzle rooms. 
          The intention behind this project was to display that unconventional perspectives can still provide a great sense of immersion and enjoyment to players
          despite being often overlooked by the heightened agency that conventional perspectives such as First and Third-Person provide within games.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="project-section" aria-labelledby="worked-on-title">
				<h2 id="worked-on-title">What I worked on:</h2>
				<ul class="project-list">
					<li>Everything, except for the 2D and 3D Art, I suck at those.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="project-section" aria-labelledby="highlights-title">
				<h2 id="highlights-title">Technical highlights:</h2>
				<p>
					This Project was the first time I decided to give additive scene loading a go. It was a concept I learnt about during my 
					first Game Jam, but didn't truly understand why the Lead Programmer used it or what it was for. After making use of this
					style of scene loading for this project, it made much more sense to me as to how useful it can be for loading and unloading
					scenes and small levels such as the ones in this project.
				</p>

				<pre><code>{`AsyncOperation loadOp = SceneManager.LoadSceneAsync(sceneName, LoadSceneMode.Additive);
        while (!loadOp.isDone)
        {
            yield return null;
        }

        Scene loadedScene = SceneManager.GetSceneByName(sceneName);
        if (loadedScene.IsValid() && loadedScene.isLoaded)
        {
            SceneManager.SetActiveScene(loadedScene);
            currentLevelSceneName = sceneName;

            if(loadedScene.name != levelSceneNames[0] && currentLevelIndex != introDuplicateSceneIndex)
            {
                batteryManager.SetBatteryFull();
                signalManager.EnableSignalChecks();
            }

            if(loadedScene.name == levelSceneNames[0] && currentLevelIndex == introDuplicateSceneIndex)
            {
                signalManager.DisableSignalChecks();
            }
        }
        else
        {
            Debug.LogError($"LevelLoadManager: Failed to load scene '{sceneName}'.");
        }`}</code></pre>

			<p>
				Explain what this code does, what problem it solves, and why it demonstrates your technical knowledge.
			</p>
			</section>

			<section class="project-section" aria-labelledby="challenges-title">
				<h2 id="challenges-title">Challenges / learnings:</h2>
				<p>
					Write about the challenges you faced during development and what you learned from them.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="project-section" aria-labelledby="links-title">
				<h2 id="links-title">Game Build & Other Links:</h2>
				<ul class="project-links">
					<li>
						<a href="https://steveybr.itch.io/hardwhere" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
							Itch.io Build
						</a>
					</li>
          <li>
            <p>
            2D Art & Illustrations provided by 
              <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/isabella-salgadox/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                Isabella Salgado
              </a>
            </p>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="project-section" aria-labelledby="dissertation-title">
				<h2 id="dissertation-title">Dissertation:</h2>
				<p>
					I had to write a dissertation for this project, it is kind of long and maybe not super interesting, but it got an 81% and I feel like it would be a waste if I didn't include it somewhere here, you know?
				</p>

				<div class="project-pdf-wrap">
					<iframe
						class="project-pdf"
						src="/HardWhereDissertation.pdf"
						title="HardWhere dissertation PDF"
					></iframe>
				</div>

			</section>
		</main>

		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.project-hero {
		position: relative;
		overflow: hidden;
		margin-top: 1.25rem;
		padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
		border-radius: 18px;
		border: 2px solid var(--border-color);
		background: var(--content-bg, transparent);
		width: min(1100px, calc(100vw - 2rem));
		left: 50%;
		transform: translateX(-50%);
		min-height: 300px;
	}

	.project-hero-video {
		position: absolute;
		inset: 0;
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
		object-fit: cover;
		filter: blur(5px) brightness(0.55) saturate(1.1);
		transform: scale(1.08);
	}

	.project-hero-overlay {
		position: absolute;
		inset: 0;
		background: linear-gradient(
			90deg,
			rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.62),
			rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25)
		);
	}

	.project-hero-content {
		position: relative;
		z-index: 1;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		min-height: 300px;
		padding: 1.5rem;
	}

	.project-title-image {
		display: block;
		max-width: min(82%, 680px);
		max-height: 200px;
		width: auto;
		height: auto;
		object-fit: contain;
	}

	.project-section {
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}

	.project-summary {
		text-align: center;
		max-width: 850px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
	}

	.project-video-wrap {
		position: relative;
		width: 100%;
		aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
		border-radius: 16px;
		overflow: hidden;
		border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
		background: #000;
	}

	.project-video {
		position: absolute;
		inset: 0;
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
		border: 0;
	}

	.project-tags {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	.project-tag {
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 0.35rem 0.8rem;
		border-radius: 999px;
		background: rgba(35, 55, 255, 0.12);
		color: var(--accent);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		border: 1px solid rgba(35, 55, 255, 0.18);
	}

	pre {
	padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
	border-radius: 12px;
	overflow-x: auto;
	font-size: 0.85rem;
	line-height: 1.5;

	border: 4px solid var(--border-color);
	}

	.project-list,
	.project-links {
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
	}

	.project-pdf-wrap {
		width: 100%;
		height: 800px;
		border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
		border-radius: 16px;
		overflow: hidden;
		background: #fff;
	}

	.project-pdf {
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
		border: 0;
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.project-hero {
			padding: 1.25rem 1rem;
			min-height: 220px;
		}

		.project-hero-content {
			min-height: 220px;
			padding: 1rem;
		}

		.project-title-image {
			max-width: 90%;
			max-height: 120px;
		}

		.project-pdf-wrap {
			height: 500px;
		}
	}
</style>